WEBVTT

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:26.750
He's overworked.

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:31.670
He had an anemia attack, but he didn't faint.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:33.130
He's sleeping.

00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:35.460
Sleeping?

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:11.980
<b><i>Run with the Wind</i></b>

00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:15.940
Thank you.

00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:24.750
Being stuck with a syringe didn't wake him up.

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:26.200
He must be really exhausted.

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:29.590
It's hard to tell when he actually sleeps.

00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:32.360
I thought he was fine without sleep.

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:34.090
It's not just practice.

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:37.510
He was doing all the cooking, too.

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:40.980
It's my fault.

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:48.230
I made him worry.

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:50.220
You know that's not true.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:53.140
I caused him much more concern.

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:54.760
No, I...

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:55.900
It was everyone.

00:02:56.900 --> 00:03:00.110
All of us can think of something we did.

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:09.000
Coach.

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:11.980
Please stop. It's ominous.

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:17.340
I don't know what to do in times like these.

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:20.880
You don't need to do anything.

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:27.410
We should run practice
ourselves tomorrow, right?

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:29.020
I agree.

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:34.680
Come to think of it, clerical procedures
like registering for meets

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:39.610
were all Haiji's job, too.

00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:45.570
Supervisor-cum-coach-cum-
manager-cum-dorm leader, huh?

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:52.980
We should at least take turns cooking.

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:56.420
Yeah. All I can cook is ochazuke, though.

00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:59.370
Me, too. I've only ever boiled pasta.

00:04:00.570 --> 00:04:04.390
Can we survive without Haiji?

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:07.810
Why don't you reconcile?

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:10.960
I mean you guys.

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:14.190
Quit the team if you can't run fast enough?

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:16.800
This is no time to be saying that.

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:20.530
I'm not the one who suggested it.

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:23.490
You're his senior.

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:26.570
I was just expressing my misgivings.

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:27.690
Hey!

00:04:27.690 --> 00:04:31.290
If that's what you hurled at me,
then you're being a nuisance.

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:34.500
Earlier, you said you made him worry.

00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:37.140
You are making him worry, aren't you?

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:39.920
That's enough!

00:04:42.140 --> 00:04:46.220
Don't ruin what Haiji entrusted to you.

00:04:46.490 --> 00:04:48.680
You make it sound like he's dead!

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:53.990
You guys sure you don't actually get along?

00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:16.350
That's not good enough, Prince.

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:21.670
<b><i>Our Speed</i></b>

00:05:24.850 --> 00:05:27.610
What? Give me a break.

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:29.180
Please.

00:05:29.530 --> 00:05:32.620
I can't even be a substitute captain.

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:35.640
We never decided who'd do it.

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:39.200
I believe that, as the eldest
and most experienced,

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:41.770
you're the most suitable candidate.

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:46.160
I just can't. I can't afford
to look after others.

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:48.860
Then... Yuki.

00:05:49.260 --> 00:05:51.370
I thought you'd ask.

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:53.020
But I refuse.

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:54.240
<b>Heart</b>

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:54.240
Was that...

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:55.730
Aw, shucks...

00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:57.080
What are you doing?

00:05:57.080 --> 00:06:00.880
You mean you don't know about "but I refuse?"

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:05.500
Just so you know, I still don't
think we can make it to Hakone.

00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:08.090
I wouldn't know how to lead the team.

00:06:08.540 --> 00:06:10.680
You're still saying that?

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:12.550
After participating in all these practices?

00:06:12.550 --> 00:06:15.140
Shut up. No. Ask someone else.

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:16.600
Then...

00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:19.610
Kakeru, how about you?

00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:21.140
Hey! What about me?

00:06:21.140 --> 00:06:23.440
If you go in order, I'm next.

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:26.330
There's no way you'd want to do it.

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:29.330
I still want to be asked.

00:06:29.330 --> 00:06:31.060
Be asked and decline.

00:06:31.060 --> 00:06:34.700
Give me the chance to act like your senior.

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:37.010
I can't respect him, at all.

00:06:37.010 --> 00:06:37.910
Yeah.

00:06:38.360 --> 00:06:40.120
I don't mind.

00:06:41.870 --> 00:06:42.830
What?

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:48.670
I may not be gentle.

00:07:05.860 --> 00:07:08.320
<b>Complete and 
Total Rest</b>

00:07:05.860 --> 00:07:08.320
<b>Joji & Jota</b>

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:10.280
<b>Plum Ochazuke</b>

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:12.240
<b>Get well soon!</b>

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:12.240
<b>I'm sorry 
for always relying on you 
for everything! 
Get well soon.
Sugiyama Takashi</b>

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:12.240
<b>This African mask 
will protect you 
from evil!
Musa Kamara</b>

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:12.240
<b>You need to rest!! 
They said eating meat when you're sick 
is good for you
King</b>

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:12.240
<b>Sorry. Get some rest!!
Sleep well, rest well.
Yuki</b>

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:12.240
<b>Take care.
Kurahara</b>

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:12.240
<b>I'll lend you 
some of my comics.
Kashiwazaki</b>

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:12.240
<b>Have some porridge!
Jota & Joji</b>

00:07:13.380 --> 00:07:14.700
Is this torture?

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:20.210
You don't have to do this.

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:20.910
What?

00:07:21.700 --> 00:07:24.740
You don't have to do what Haiji does.

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:27.590
If I leave you alone, you'll fall
farther and farther behind.

00:07:28.390 --> 00:07:30.540
Everyone else's pace is increasing.

00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:33.980
Their efforts will be ruined because of you.

00:07:33.980 --> 00:07:36.500
Buck up and take this seriously.

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:40.220
Since when have you been fast?

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:41.380
Huh?

00:07:42.050 --> 00:07:43.850
Since you were a child?

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:45.890
Probably. After all, you're a prodigy.

00:07:45.890 --> 00:07:47.020
That's not true.

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:51.800
Then try talking at my speed.

00:07:59.470 --> 00:08:01.060
What is this?

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:02.790
Hey, twins!

00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:04.540
What is it?

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:07.650
We made lots. Eat all you want.

00:08:08.610 --> 00:08:10.640
Why did you start reading comics
as soon as we got home?

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:12.260
You should get changed first.

00:08:12.260 --> 00:08:14.890
I need to read the magazine that
came out today by the end of the day.

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:17.100
Your comics aren't going
anywhere. Get changed.

00:08:17.480 --> 00:08:19.520
Freshness is everything!

00:08:19.910 --> 00:08:20.860
What?

00:08:21.880 --> 00:08:23.260
He's right!

00:08:24.260 --> 00:08:26.150
Freshness is everything!

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:30.480
I heard Haiji collapsed,
so I brought you something.

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:35.880
Hana, perfect timing!

00:08:35.880 --> 00:08:37.620
I missed you!

00:08:38.130 --> 00:08:40.490
Huh? Uh, um... What?

00:08:40.490 --> 00:08:42.000
Can you cook?

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:44.050
Huh?

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:54.470
<b>Bathroom</b>

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:54.470
Musa!

00:08:54.900 --> 00:08:56.190
Hurry!

00:08:56.930 --> 00:08:58.390
Hurry up!

00:08:58.390 --> 00:08:59.850
<b>Bathroom</b>

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:10.830
S-Save me...

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:15.410
Musa!

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:20.240
I-I'm sorry. Maybe it wasn't to their tastes.

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:21.620
What do you two think?

00:09:21.620 --> 00:09:23.220
It's good.

00:09:23.220 --> 00:09:24.830
I'm glad.

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:28.290
Whenever I cook at home, everyone says it's good.

00:09:28.290 --> 00:09:31.680
My dad cries every time he eats it.

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:32.500
Really?

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:41.210
He must be better after a full day of rest.

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:42.310
<b>Complete and Total Rest</b>

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:42.310
<b>Joji 
& 
Jota</b>

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:43.460
Excuse the intrusion.

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:46.350
Haiji?

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:48.590
He vanished?!

00:09:48.590 --> 00:09:49.650
How?

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:51.060
We missed something.

00:09:51.060 --> 00:09:52.770
Unbelievably enough,

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:55.050
there was a window in his room!

00:09:55.490 --> 00:09:56.490
Oh...

00:09:56.930 --> 00:10:00.530
In other words, Haiji opened the
window and used it to get outside.

00:10:00.530 --> 00:10:03.280
His room's on the first floor.
It must've been easy.

00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:06.590
We were stupid to let them handle it.

00:10:06.590 --> 00:10:08.110
What? Why?

00:10:08.110 --> 00:10:09.910
Where did he go?

00:10:09.910 --> 00:10:11.240
I don't know.

00:10:11.240 --> 00:10:14.320
He finished the ochazuke
we left in his room this morning.

00:10:15.100 --> 00:10:18.430
So, he's well enough to eat 
and escape through a window?

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:20.850
Then he must be fine.

00:10:20.850 --> 00:10:22.640
It's over.

00:10:34.990 --> 00:10:37.330
You didn't need to come all the way here.

00:10:37.330 --> 00:10:40.230
It's fine. Thank you.

00:10:41.430 --> 00:10:44.160
Hey. I came to thank him for yesterday.

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:46.660
You're a fine man.

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:47.380
Right?

00:10:47.380 --> 00:10:49.690
What? Oh, no.

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:59.260
You totally lost that argument.

00:10:59.770 --> 00:11:01.760
It's no laughing matter.

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:04.380
There's no beating Prince
when it comes to sophistry.

00:11:04.810 --> 00:11:06.370
Not that it is.

00:11:08.130 --> 00:11:11.050
Try talking at my speed, huh?

00:11:11.560 --> 00:11:13.170
Will he be all right?

00:11:14.430 --> 00:11:15.460
Prince.

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:20.780
I got a proper look for the first time
today, but he has no form at all.

00:11:21.220 --> 00:11:23.120
He needs to be corrected.

00:11:24.360 --> 00:11:26.430
You got a proper look for the first time, huh?

00:11:28.530 --> 00:11:30.150
I...

00:11:30.150 --> 00:11:34.560
I'm not criticizing you.
You had your own problems.

00:11:36.080 --> 00:11:42.060
But I think he was watching you and
waiting to see when you'd look his way.

00:11:43.860 --> 00:11:45.670
You're always facing forwards.

00:11:48.420 --> 00:11:49.740
Prince isn't the only one.

00:11:50.620 --> 00:11:53.340
Everyone else is running behind you.

00:11:53.340 --> 00:11:57.800
Until you turn around, you'll never
see them from where you are.

00:11:59.190 --> 00:12:03.050
You won't see who is running where and how.

00:12:19.980 --> 00:12:20.800
Let's go home.

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:24.050
I've only had ochazuke to eat today.

00:12:25.100 --> 00:12:27.470
I think I might get even more sick.

00:12:44.530 --> 00:12:47.840
We can finally eat a decent meal.

00:12:47.840 --> 00:12:49.760
Sorry for making you guys worry.

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:54.250
Don't be shy. Eat all you want today.

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:55.450
Haiji!

00:12:55.450 --> 00:12:57.230
Welcome home!

00:12:57.230 --> 00:12:58.500
By the way,

00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:01.340
I heard Hana made breakfast.

00:13:01.810 --> 00:13:04.930
She even brought her own ingredients.

00:13:05.350 --> 00:13:08.170
I'd better thank her later.

00:13:08.170 --> 00:13:09.000
Huh?

00:13:09.860 --> 00:13:11.580
What's wrong, guys?

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:15.810
<b>204

00:13:16.970 --> 00:13:17.770
What?

00:13:18.490 --> 00:13:23.740
I said, could you lend me some
comics you recommend?

00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:28.700
No, I—I don't have anything in my room.

00:13:29.670 --> 00:13:30.900
I thought once in a while...

00:13:30.900 --> 00:13:32.560
Do you mind romance?

00:13:34.550 --> 00:13:35.490
What?

00:13:46.040 --> 00:13:48.010
You're really good at that.

00:13:48.010 --> 00:13:52.510
Really? It's pretty hard to keep it steady.

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:05.420
That's it!

00:14:05.420 --> 00:14:06.220
Huh?

00:14:13.460 --> 00:14:15.060
You're making fun of me, aren't you?

00:14:15.060 --> 00:14:16.410
No, I'm serious.

00:14:17.090 --> 00:14:19.530
What? You're going to run like that?

00:14:19.530 --> 00:14:21.020
It's dangerous.

00:14:21.020 --> 00:14:24.120
It'll be fine. I just want to try it for a bit.

00:14:24.120 --> 00:14:26.270
Then, I'll lead the way.

00:14:26.900 --> 00:14:28.070
Please do.

00:14:29.010 --> 00:14:31.260
That's it. That's it, Prince.

00:14:31.260 --> 00:14:35.970
<b>Hijiki</b>

00:14:31.860 --> 00:14:35.970
Normally, you look down when you read comics.

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:39.120
But when you're on the treadmill,

00:14:39.120 --> 00:14:42.840
you naturally look forwards 
since your comics are in front of you.

00:14:43.720 --> 00:14:47.630
You stand up straighter than
you do when you're just running.

00:14:47.630 --> 00:14:49.350
It brings your center of gravity forwards.

00:14:49.350 --> 00:14:50.360
What?

00:14:51.460 --> 00:14:53.120
Good pace, right?

00:14:53.500 --> 00:14:54.580
Maybe.

00:14:54.860 --> 00:14:57.880
Then could you turn the pages, too?

00:14:57.880 --> 00:15:00.630
And could I try something else?

00:15:10.240 --> 00:15:12.140
This is amazing, Prince.

00:15:12.420 --> 00:15:14.100
It's totally different.

00:15:14.100 --> 00:15:15.720
You're totally different.

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:20.480
With my bangs out of my face, I can
see what's in front of me a lot better.

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:22.020
Yes.

00:15:22.780 --> 00:15:24.890
What have you been looking at until now?

00:15:25.970 --> 00:15:29.770
Try imagining a comic
in front of you as you run.

00:15:39.640 --> 00:15:42.020
There's a lot I'd like to say about that.

00:15:42.020 --> 00:15:45.390
I bet it'd be fun if you
put bells in his hands.

00:15:45.390 --> 00:15:47.510
Why does he do that?

00:15:47.510 --> 00:15:50.000
I know! It's like when he's reading comics!

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:50.720
Oh!

00:15:51.230 --> 00:15:57.280
Yes. Prince's arms are fixed in a reading
position even when he's running.

00:15:57.280 --> 00:16:00.930
Now that I think about it, 
I'm amazed he could run like that.

00:16:02.050 --> 00:16:04.600
Since we're not short-distance runners,

00:16:04.600 --> 00:16:07.150
there's no need for sweeping arm movements.

00:16:07.910 --> 00:16:11.040
But I'd like to fix his habit
of holding them in place.

00:16:12.850 --> 00:16:15.660
Hey, it's starting to look right.

00:16:16.060 --> 00:16:18.540
"I can't wait to go back to my room and read!"

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:20.040
Imagine that as you run.

00:16:20.560 --> 00:16:23.460
I can't wait to go back to my room and read.

00:16:23.760 --> 00:16:26.610
Yes, that's it. Keep it up.

00:16:26.610 --> 00:16:28.970
You've got your color back.

00:16:28.970 --> 00:16:29.920
Huh?

00:16:30.400 --> 00:16:31.720
I've been eating.

00:16:31.720 --> 00:16:33.880
I don't want to make you worry unnecessarily.

00:16:34.510 --> 00:16:35.580
Thank you.

00:16:36.170 --> 00:16:38.610
You don't miss a thing.

00:16:38.610 --> 00:16:42.310
What about them?
You could've intervened anytime.

00:16:42.740 --> 00:16:45.520
Did you stay out of it because
you knew this would happen?

00:16:45.830 --> 00:16:47.440
No way.

00:16:47.440 --> 00:16:50.160
I intended to fix things if I had to.

00:16:50.160 --> 00:16:55.630
But I didn't think it'd ever really be his
if he'd learned to run that way.

00:16:56.790 --> 00:16:59.060
It's truly a fortunate error.

00:16:59.990 --> 00:17:02.370
"I wish I could go back to my room and read!"

00:17:02.370 --> 00:17:03.080
Now you!

00:17:03.080 --> 00:17:06.290
I wish I could go back to my room and read!

00:17:09.650 --> 00:17:11.020
Ow...

00:17:32.900 --> 00:17:34.110
Go, Prince!

00:17:34.110 --> 00:17:36.150
Final spurt!

00:17:46.970 --> 00:17:48.550
Prince!

00:17:48.550 --> 00:17:50.130
Prince!

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:11.940
Whoa!

00:18:12.290 --> 00:18:16.190
This is amazing. 
Is Kakeru going to break 14:30?

00:18:33.660 --> 00:18:35.210
Prince!

00:18:37.170 --> 00:18:39.130
Forward!

00:18:41.460 --> 00:18:42.550
Face forward.

00:18:42.550 --> 00:18:44.010
Forward!

00:18:45.470 --> 00:18:48.180
Hey! Why's he slowing down?

00:18:48.180 --> 00:18:50.650
He was going to get a good time, too!

00:18:51.790 --> 00:18:52.940
Kakeru...

00:18:55.570 --> 00:18:56.780
Prince!

00:19:00.750 --> 00:19:03.330
I am... facing forward...

00:19:03.330 --> 00:19:06.830
You never... shut up!

00:19:07.890 --> 00:19:11.310
I'm fine.

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:13.130
Go!

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:26.940
Prince!

00:19:29.240 --> 00:19:30.330
Prince!

00:19:31.100 --> 00:19:33.020
Hey, he might make it.

00:19:33.020 --> 00:19:34.310
Yeah, he just might.

00:19:34.310 --> 00:19:36.350
You can do it, Prince!

00:19:37.180 --> 00:19:38.780
Prince!

00:19:39.140 --> 00:19:42.250
Final spurt!

00:20:02.090 --> 00:20:04.050
Yeah!

00:20:07.730 --> 00:20:08.810
Prince!

00:20:10.020 --> 00:20:11.980
You did it. You made it.

00:20:13.270 --> 00:20:14.470
Don't make such a fuss.

00:20:15.250 --> 00:20:16.940
I still have a long way to go.

00:20:16.940 --> 00:20:19.700
Yes, you do. You can go much faster.

00:20:19.700 --> 00:20:20.880
Shut up!

00:20:20.880 --> 00:20:23.840
What's so great about that?

00:20:24.420 --> 00:20:25.700
Who knows?

00:20:28.390 --> 00:20:31.710
